-- title:
--   Rational places are centred at closed special points
-- statement:
--   The statement is set in the Igusa base-model frame for the full-level modular function field, and its content is the existence of a centre on the special fibre for every rational place.
--
--   **Ambient data.** A prime $q$ with $5 \le q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, which by `hW` consists of exactly the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, i.e. the places $w$ that are rational, affine geometric, and whose value at the generic $j$-invariant lies in the supersingular set `ssJSet q` (the set of $j$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve with that invariant has no nontrivial $q$-torsion point); the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full modular function field of level $M'$ inside Laurent series) into `fieldBar q M' = xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2M') (levelH q M')`; a constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` — so a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal, a place map preserving degrees and compatible with divisors, and the compatibility `algebraMap_mem_iff` with $A$ — together with `hR₀`, asserting that any Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` belongs to `R₀.integers` and has $R_0$-residue equal to the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$; an index $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$); and two families of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'`, namely $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$.
--
--   **Igusa-component hypotheses.** `hIg_inf` describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the line `lineInfty q`: an element $f$ belongs to it precisely when $f$, viewed as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is a quotient $x/y$ of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose denominator $y$ has nonzero coefficientwise reduction. `hIg` asserts that every line $\ell$ is of the form $\overline{\gamma}\cdot\infty$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`. `hIg_inj` asserts injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, and `hIg_perm` that for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   **Supersingular-component hypotheses.** `hSS_A` states that, for each $s \in W$, an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ (after the constant embedding) if and only if it lies in $A$. `hSS_over` states: for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` such that $f$ has nonnegative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the element $j$ (the $q$-expansion `coeffEmb jq`, regarded inside `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`) has nonnegative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and moreover for every $a \in A$ whose residue in `ResidueField A` equals the value of $s$ at the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and the constant $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$. `hSS_fix` states that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and `hSS_tr` that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$. Further, $R$ is a regular prolongation of `fieldBar q M'` along $A$ with values in `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2M') (levelH q M')`, with `hR` identifying `R.integers` with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and `hR₀O` stating that $f \in$ `R₀.integers` holds exactly when the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   **Arithmetic hypotheses on $A$ and on the base field.** An element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that the contraction $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); and `hκ`, stating that every element of $A$ differs from some element of $k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. An auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ with $A_1 = A \cap K_1$ (`hA₁`), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   **Quantification in the conclusion.** The field `fieldBar q M'` is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every finite family $c_i \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a_i$ in the compositum $K'F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$ (linear disjointness of $F_0$ from the constants); and every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose underlying Laurent series has rational coefficients lies in $F_0$. Put $K_1F_0$ for the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$. The assertion is further made for every $A_1$-algebra structure on $K_1F_0$ whose structure map agrees with the inclusion of $K_1$ into `fieldBar q M'`, and for every $j_1 \in K_1F_0$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the $q$-expansion of the $j$-function, $j_1$ being nonzero; under the hypothesis that the structure morphism `TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase A₁ (K₁F₀) j₁` from the two-chart integral model — the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring of elements of $K_1F_0$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring of elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$ — to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ is proper.
--
--   **Abbreviations introduced.** For a point $x$ of the model and $f \in K_1F_0$: `InStalk x f` says that for each point $y$ of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ mapping to $x$ there are $g, h$ in the finite chart algebra with $h \notin y$ and $fh = g$, and likewise for the chart at infinity; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$ in each chart. For a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational (the structure map from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to the residue field of $P$ is surjective) and that for every $f \in K_1F_0$ with `InStalk x f` the image of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$, the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$, and $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ if and only if `InMax x f` holds. A fourth abbreviation `GoodPt` is also introduced, asking of a point $x$ that it lie over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$, be maximal for specialisation, that in each chart every element of the chart algebra whose image is a non-unit of `R.integers` lie in the prime corresponding to a preimage of $x$, and that for each preimage $y$ in the finite chart and each homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ avoid `ssJSet q`; the conclusion does not refer to `GoodPt`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is rational, there exists a point $x$ of the two-chart integral model such that: (i) the image of $x$ under the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ is the closed point; (ii) $x$ is closed in the sense that every $y$ to which $x$ specialises equals $x$; and (iii) `Centred P x` holds, i.e. $P$ is rational and every $f \in K_1F_0$ lying in the stalk at $x$ in the above chartwise sense satisfies $f \in \mathcal O_P$, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ has $A$-valuation less than $1$ exactly when $f$ lies in the maximal ideal at $x$ in the above chartwise sense.
--
--   This is the existence half of the valuative criterion of properness, applied to the two-chart integral model of the full-level modular curve over the henselian discrete valuation ring $A_1$: each rational place of the function field acquires a centre on the special fibre, compatibly with the valuation of $A$. It is used in the analysis of the reduction map on places, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_goodPt_of_centred_of_not_mem_range_iotaFin_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_goodPt_of_centred_of_not_mem_range_iotaFin_twoChartIntegralModel) and by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_twoChartIntegralModel_of_forall_not_ssTube`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_twoChartIntegralModel_of_forall_not_ssTube).
